<p>For 6 years or so, I have been down the custom, split, ergonomic keyboard rabbit hole.  And, since running a few different boards, I have found what I like and dislike in a board - to the point that it sounded like a good idea to build one that ticked all the boxes of preferences - 34 keys, MX switches, wired (more reliable than battery and stops the need to charge occasionally).  I had my eye on a few, and decided on the <a href="https://github.com/icyphox/ferricy">Ferricy</a>.  This will be a bit of a build log as to my findings, the parts list, and how it all came together.</p>
